*> Implementation test of formats/src/sha256.cob (SHA256-INIT, SHA256-UPDATE, SHA256-FINAL; 22 §7.2):
*> the FIPS 180-4 vectors (abc, the empty string, the 56-byte two-block message), a message given in
*> pieces of every size, a message of 1000 bytes in 7-byte pieces, a context that is reused after FINAL,
*> and the context state (open after INIT, NULL and idle after FINAL, a 32-byte digest).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-SHA256.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY FORMATS.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-DIGEST-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG VALUE 32.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(64).
 01 WS-THOUSAND            PIC X(1000).
 01 WS-POS                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PIECE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SHOWN               PIC -(9)9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "abc" TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "sha256 of abc (FIPS 180-4)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "sha256 digest is 32 bytes: the hex of 64 digits ends the shown text" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "64" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX(65:64)
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-HEX)) TO WS-SHOWN
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOWN) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "sha256 of the empty string" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "sha256 of an update of 0 bytes is the empty digest" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The 56-byte message of two blocks, in one call and as 1 + 55 bytes.
     MOVE "abcdbcdecdefdefgefghfghighijhijkijkljklmklmnlmnomnopnopq" TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 56 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "sha256 of the 56-byte two-block message" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "248d6a61d20638b8e5c026930c3e6039a33ce45964ff2167f6ecedd419db06c1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     MOVE 1 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
     MOVE 55 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-TEXT(2:55) WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "sha256 of the same message in pieces of 1 and 55 bytes" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   1000 bytes of a, in pieces of 7 bytes (the last one shorter).
     MOVE ALL "a" TO WS-THOUSAND
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     MOVE 1 TO WS-POS
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-POS > 1000
         COMPUTE WS-PIECE = FUNCTION MIN(7, 1001 - WS-POS)
         CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-THOUSAND(WS-POS:WS-PIECE) WS-PIECE
         ADD WS-PIECE TO WS-POS
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "sha256 of 1000 bytes of a given in pieces of 7" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "41edece42d63e8d9bf515a9ba6932e1c20cbc9f5a5d134645adb5db1b9737ea3" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The context: NULL and idle before INIT and after FINAL, open between; reusable.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     MOVE "sha256 INIT leaves the context open (state 1, pointer set)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FMSHA-STATE = 1 AND FMSHA-CTX NOT = NULL
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     MOVE "sha256 FINAL frees the context (state 0, pointer NULL)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FMSHA-STATE = 0 AND FMSHA-CTX = NULL
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "abc" TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA FMSHA-DIGEST
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING FMSHA-DIGEST WS-DIGEST-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "sha256 of abc again with the same context record" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-HEX(1:64) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-SHA256.
 COPY FMTEST.
